      "message": "In aosp/4232683 (`pkvm_host_use_dma()`), we use `PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_BORROWED` in `host_mmu` PTEs to mark MMIO/reserved pages that cannot be donated, whereas here we use `PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_OWNED` for `ramoops`.\n\nHaving two different states for this increases the total canonical MMIO meta-states from `4` to `5` (in go/page-custody-battles), even though both represent the exact same invariant in the MMIO state machine (a host-accessible `is_mmio_range()` page that is permanently non-exclusive / non-donatable).\n\nCould we use the same page state for both (`PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_OWNED` or `PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_BORROWED`) so we keep the MMIO state space at `4` states? (`PKVM_PAGE_SHARED_OWNED` arguably fits both better since `PKVM_ID_HOST` is the owner sharing the range, though either works as long as both patches use the same state, just noting that in `pkvm_host_use_dma()` we should avoid overwriting `ramoops`\u0027s `WB` memtype with `host_mmu_pte_prot(true, true)` (`UC`) if an already-shared page is skipped in the check loop.)",
